https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs:
HTML provides a [`crossorigin`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/img#crossorigin) attribute for images that, in combination with an appropriate [CORS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/CORS) header, allows images defined by the [`<img>`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/img) element that are loaded from foreign origins to be used in a [`<canvas>`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/canvas) as if they had been loaded from the current origin.
